{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5", "id": "msg_011Cf4zyacRQwHAuGWNcDsjm", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**2 captures.**\n\n| Capture | Mode | Feeds |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Mode A-visit** (persona-driven visit \u2014 `traversal-visit`) | clarity, conversion, trust |\n| 2 | **Mode C** (session-less crawl \u2014 `traversal-crawl`) | seo |\n\nThe arithmetic: your four objectives collapse into two capture modes, not four. Clarity, conversion and trust are all scored off the *same* A-visit evidence \u2014 one persona walking the site with a question, producing screenshots, session log, timeline and debrief. Three lenses read that one body of evidence afterwards. SEO can't reuse it, because it needs a no-persona, no-session crawl recording per-page markup facts (titles, meta, canonicals, headings, structured data, internal links, robots, sitemap) \u2014 different driver, different output shape.\n\nSo: 2 captures, 4 scoring passes.\n\nOne dependency worth naming up front, since it's the only thing that changes the number: **captures scale per persona, lenses don't.** If the interview lands on one persona, it stays at 2. Two personas means two A-visit captures (4 lenses\u2026 still 1 crawl), so 3 captures total. The Mode C crawl is always exactly 1 regardless \u2014 it has no persona to vary.\n\nAlso note conversion specifically requires a stated conversion goal in the target file. Without one that lens has nothing to measure against, but it doesn't add a capture \u2014 it's a prerequisite on capture 1, not a third capture.\n\nNothing started, nothing asked."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 140, "cache_read_input_tokens": 21007, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 140}, "output_tokens": 9, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "75b5217a-ab2d-4a1b-8e27-da39219a4641", "uuid": "c62421da-ee38-4ada-b464-38bff314cad4", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T09:37:40.420Z", "request_id": "req_011Cf4zya7tjAXrq9aFJb1Yy"}
